{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.NormalForms","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.NormalForms","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.CompositionLemma","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Lex","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":68,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.DistAlgGenerators.num_generators","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.DistAlgGenerators.num_generators","kind":"def","line":717,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L717-L717","doc":"The number of Lie algebra generators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.DistAlgGenerators.p_prime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.DistAlgGenerators.p_prime","kind":"theorem","line":715,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L715-L715","doc":"`p` is prime. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.DistAlgGenerators.p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.DistAlgGenerators.p","kind":"def","line":713,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L713-L713","doc":"The prime characteristic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.DistAlgGenerators.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.DistAlgGenerators.mk","kind":"ctor","line":711,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L711-L711","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.DistAlgGenerators","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.DistAlgGenerators","kind":"structure","line":707,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L707-L717","doc":"The generators of the distribution algebra `Dist(G)` in\ncharacteristic `p`.  These are the divided-power generators\n`x^{(n)} = x^n / n!` for each generator `x` of the Lie algebra,\ntruncated at `p`-th powers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.pbw_monomials_are_not_all_normal_forms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.pbw_monomials_are_not_all_normal_forms","kind":"theorem","line":656,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L656-L703","doc":"**⚠ The PBW normal-form claim, as it was stated, is FALSE.**\n\nThis used to be an axiom:\n\n> every `PBWMonomial` is in normal form under the `q`-Serre system\n\nwith `PBWMonomial.toMonomial m = E_+^a ++ K^{b₊} ++ K⁻¹^{b₋} ++ E_-^c`. Once\n`qSerreRewritingSystem` became a definition (§3.1) the claim became\ncheckable, and it fails. `⟨a,b₊,b₋,c⟩ = ⟨0,1,1,0⟩` is the word `[K, K⁻¹]`,\nwhich is *exactly* rule 1's leading monomial, so it is reducible.\n\nThe axiom's own justification is where it went wrong. It argued that the PBW\nword \"contains no forbidden subword … because generators appear in canonical\norder with each block homogeneous\" — but the `K` block is immediately\nfollowed by the `K⁻¹` block, which produces `[K, K⁻¹]` whenever both are\nnon-empty. Homogeneity within blocks says nothing about the joins between\nthem, and there are three bad joins, not one:\n\n| join | when | is the lm of |\n|---|---|---|\n| `[K, K⁻¹]` | `b₊ ≥ 1` and `b₋ ≥ 1` | rule 1 |\n| `[K, E_-]` | `b₊ ≥ 1` and `c ≥ 1` | rule 4 |\n| `[E_+, E_-]` | `a ≥ 1`, `b₊ = b₋ = 0`, `c ≥ 1` | rule 5 |\n\nSo the letter order `E_+ … K … E_- ` is not the normal-form order for this\nsystem at all. Reading the rules' orientations off §3.1, reduction moves\n`E_-` left past `E_+` (rule 5) and moves `K` right past both (rules 3, 4), so\nthe normal words are `E_-^c E_+^a K^b` — with `K` and `K⁻¹` never mixed.\n\nNothing downstream is left resting on the false claim: `ugb_pbw_corollary`\nnow takes normality as an explicit hypothesis rather than importing it from\nhere. Establishing it for the corrected shape is open, and is the genuine\nremaining content of Bokut–Malcolmson Thm 3.2.\n\nReference: Bokut & Malcolmson, Israel J. Math. 96 (1996), Theorem 3.2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.pbwElement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.pbwElement","kind":"def","line":650,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L650-L654","doc":"The element of `k⟨SU2Gen⟩` supported on a single PBW word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.pbw_word_K_Kinv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.pbw_word_K_Kinv","kind":"theorem","line":645,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L645-L648","doc":"The `PBWMonomial` with `b₊ = b₋ = 1` and `a = c = 0` is the word `[K, K⁻¹]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.PBWMonomial.toMonomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.PBWMonomial.toMonomial","kind":"def","line":638,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L638-L643","doc":"The PBW monomial as an explicit word in the generators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.PBWMonomial.c","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.PBWMonomial.c","kind":"def","line":636,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L636-L636","doc":"Exponent of `E_-`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.PBWMonomial.b_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.PBWMonomial.b_neg","kind":"def","line":634,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L634-L634","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.PBWMonomial.b_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.PBWMonomial.b_pos","kind":"def","line":633,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L633-L633","doc":"Exponent of `K` (can be negative, represented as `b₊ - b₋`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.PBWMonomial.a","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.PBWMonomial.a","kind":"def","line":631,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L631-L631","doc":"Exponent of `E_+`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.PBWMonomial.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.PBWMonomial.mk","kind":"ctor","line":629,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L629-L629","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.PBWMonomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.PBWMonomial","kind":"structure","line":625,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L625-L636","doc":"A **PBW monomial** is a word of the form `E_+^a · K^b · E_-^c`.\nThese are exactly the normal-form monomials under the deg-lex\norder with the `q`-Serre rewriting system: no leading monomial\nof any relation appears as a subword. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_is_gs_basis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_is_gs_basis","kind":"axiom","line":575,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L575-L621","doc":"**Theorem** (Bokut–Malcolmson 1996):\nThe `q`-Serre relations form a Gröbner–Shirshov basis for\n`U_q(su(2))` under the deg-lex order.\n\n**The overlap analysis this docstring used to carry was wrong, and the\nfive-rule system it described was not a Gröbner–Shirshov basis** (bean\nqou-18s7). It listed six \"S-polynomial computations\", of which three —\n`(1,3)`, `(1,4)`, `(3,4)` — are not ambiguities at all: those pairs share a\n*first* letter, and an overlap requires a proper **suffix** of one leading\nword to equal a proper **prefix** of the other. It also recorded `(2,3)` as\n\"no overlap\", when `[K⁻¹,K]` followed by `[K,E_+]` overlaps at `K` and is in\nfact one of the two ambiguities that **fail**.\n\nThe real analysis, computed exactly over `ℚ(q)` by\n`computations/qserre_gs_basis_check.py`:\n\n* the **five**-rule system has exactly **5** overlap ambiguities, and two of\n  them do not resolve — both decisively, with each pair of reducts genuinely\n  irreducible:\n\n  | ambiguity | word | one way | the other |\n  |---|---|---|---|\n  | R2/R3 | `K⁻¹ K E_+` | `E_+` | `q²·K⁻¹ E_+ K` |\n  | R2/R4 | `K⁻¹ K E_-` | `E_-` | `q⁻²·K⁻¹ E_- K` |\n\n  Both are instances of the same gap: nothing rewrites `K⁻¹` past `E_±`, so\n  `K⁻¹ E_± K` is stuck.\n\n* adding the two missing rules (6 and 7, the `K⁻¹` commutation rules) gives\n  **8** ambiguities, and **all 8 resolve**.\n\nSo this axiom is now stated of the **completed seven-rule system**, where the\ncritical-pair check passes. That check is a symbolic computation, not a Lean\nproof: the axiom records a verified-but-not-formalised claim, which is a\nmaterially better position than the unverified one it was in, and materially\nworse than a theorem. Formalising the eight resolutions is the way to remove\nit.\n\nHistory worth keeping: this is the third claim in this file to be examined by\nmaking it checkable, and the second to be found false — see\n`pbw_monomials_are_not_all_normal_forms` for the other.\n\nReference: Bokut & Malcolmson, Israel J. Math. 96 (1996). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_rules_monic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_rules_monic","kind":"theorem","line":555,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L555-L573","doc":"**The q-Serre rules have unit leading coefficients.**\n\nDischarges the hypothesis `ugb_pbw_corollary` had to carry while the system was\nopaque (bean qou-lzoo left it hanging deliberately rather than assert a monicity\naxiom; this proves it instead). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerreRewritingSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerreRewritingSystem","kind":"def","line":548,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L548-L553","doc":"The rewriting system derived from the `q`-Serre relations — **a definition,\nnot an axiom**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerreRules","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerreRules","kind":"def","line":540,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L540-L544","doc":"The seven rules — the five of the original presentation, **plus the two\n`K⁻¹` commutation rules it was missing**. See the completion note in §3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_rule_lc_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_rule_lc_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":520,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L520-L538","doc":"**Every q-Serre rule is monic** — each relation is written with coefficient\n`1` on its leading monomial. This is the fact `ugb_pbw_corollary` needs, and the\nreason the system had to be built rather than axiomatised. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.four_lc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.four_lc","kind":"theorem","line":511,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L511-L518","doc":"Likewise for four terms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.two_lc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.two_lc","kind":"theorem","line":503,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L503-L509","doc":"The leading coefficient of a two-term element is `c₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_lm_7","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_lm_7","kind":"theorem","line":499,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L499-L501","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_lm_6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_lm_6","kind":"theorem","line":495,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L495-L497","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_lm_5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_lm_5","kind":"theorem","line":489,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L489-L493","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_lm_4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_lm_4","kind":"theorem","line":485,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L485-L487","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_lm_3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_lm_3","kind":"theorem","line":481,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L481-L483","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_lm_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_lm_2","kind":"theorem","line":478,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L478-L479","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_lm_1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerre_lm_1","kind":"theorem","line":475,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L475-L476","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerreRule7","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerreRule7","kind":"def","line":471,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L471-L473","doc":"**Rule 7**: `K⁻¹·E_- → q²·E_-·K⁻¹`. The other missing rule. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerreRule6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerreRule6","kind":"def","line":464,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L464-L469","doc":"**Rule 6**: `K⁻¹·E_+ → q⁻²·E_+·K⁻¹`.\n\nOne of the two rules the original five were missing; without it the system\nis not confluent — see the completion note in §3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerreRule5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerreRule5","kind":"def","line":458,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L458-L462","doc":"**Rule 5**: `E_+·E_- → E_-·E_+ + (K − K⁻¹)/(q − q⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerreRule4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerreRule4","kind":"def","line":454,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L454-L456","doc":"**Rule 4**: `K·E_- → q⁻²·E_-·K`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerreRule3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerreRule3","kind":"def","line":450,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L450-L452","doc":"**Rule 3**: `K·E_+ → q²·E_+·K`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerreRule2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerreRule2","kind":"def","line":446,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L446-L448","doc":"**Rule 2**: `K⁻¹·K → 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerreRule1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.qSerreRule1","kind":"def","line":442,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L442-L444","doc":"**Rule 1**: `K·K⁻¹ → 1`, i.e. the relation `K·K⁻¹ − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.four_lm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.four_lm","kind":"theorem","line":425,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L425-L440","doc":"Likewise for four terms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.two_lm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.two_lm","kind":"theorem","line":410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L410-L423","doc":"The leading monomial of a two-term element is `m₁`, provided `m₂` is below\nit. Maximality is finite: the support has two elements. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.four_support_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.four_support_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":405,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L405-L408","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.two_support_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.two_support_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":401,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L401-L403","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.four","kind":"def","line":389,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L389-L399","doc":"A four-term algebra element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.two","kind":"def","line":379,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L379-L387","doc":"A two-term algebra element `c₁·m₁ + c₂·m₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.QSerreRelations.q_ne_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.QSerreRelations.q_ne_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":351,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L351-L351","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.QSerreRelations.q_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.QSerreRelations.q_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":350,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L350-L350","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.QSerreRelations.q_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.QSerreRelations.q_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":349,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L349-L349","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.QSerreRelations.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.QSerreRelations.q","kind":"def","line":348,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L348-L348","doc":"The deformation parameter `q ≠ 0, ±1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.QSerreRelations.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.QSerreRelations.mk","kind":"ctor","line":346,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L346-L346","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.QSerreRelations","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.QSerreRelations","kind":"structure","line":337,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L337-L351","doc":"The `q`-Serre relations defining `U_q(su(2))`:\n\n1. `K · K⁻¹ = 1`  and  `K⁻¹ · K = 1`\n2. `K · E_+ = q² · E_+ · K`\n3. `K · E_- = q⁻² · E_- · K`\n4. `E_+ · E_- − E_- · E_+ = (K − K⁻¹) / (q − q⁻¹)`\n\nEach relation is oriented so that the left-hand side has the larger\nleading monomial under deg-lex.  This yields four reduction rules. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.degLexOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.degLexOrder","kind":"def","line":325,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L325-L333","doc":"The **deg-lex admissible order** on monomials over `SU2Gen`,\nfully proved: well-founded, trichotomous, and compatible with\nconcatenation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.degLexLt_right_compat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.degLexLt_right_compat","kind":"theorem","line":313,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L313-L323","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.degLexLt_left_compat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.degLexLt_left_compat","kind":"theorem","line":297,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L297-L311","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.degLexLt_trichotomy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.degLexLt_trichotomy","kind":"theorem","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L281-L295","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.degLexLt_wf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.degLexLt_wf","kind":"theorem","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L269-L279","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.lexLt_trichotomy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.lexLt_trichotomy","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L153-L180","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.lexLt_trans","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.lexLt_trans","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L121-L151","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.lexLt_irrefl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.lexLt_irrefl","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L112-L119","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.degLexLt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.degLexLt","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L103-L110","doc":"The **deg-lex order** on monomials in `{E_+, K, K⁻¹, E_-}`:\nfirst compare by total degree (word length), then lexicographically\nusing the rank ordering `E_- < K⁻¹ < K < E_+`.\n\nThis is the standard admissible order for quantum group\nGröbner–Shirshov computations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.lexLt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.lexLt","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L93-L101","doc":"Lexicographic comparison of monomials (lists of generators) using\nthe rank function.  Compares element-wise left-to-right; shorter\nlists are smaller when one is a prefix of the other. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SU2Gen.rank_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SU2Gen.rank_injective","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L89-L91","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SU2Gen.rank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SU2Gen.rank","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L55-L87","doc":"Numeric rank of each generator for the lexicographic order:\n`E_- < E_+ < K_inv < K` (ascending).\n\n**Corrected twice, both times because the rules constrain it and nothing\nwas checking.**\n\n* qou-ix9e: originally `K = 2 < E_+ = 3`, which made rule 3's leading\n  monomial `[E_+, K]` — its own right-hand side — so the system rewrote in\n  the direction opposite to the one its docstring claimed.\n* qou-18s7: the five-rule system turned out not to be a Gröbner–Shirshov\n  basis at all (see §3), and completing it adds the two `K⁻¹` commutation\n  rules, which impose two further constraints that the previous ranking\n  violated.\n\nThe five orientation constraints, one per non-inverse rule:\n\n| rule | needs |\n|---|---|\n| 3 `K·E_+ → q²·E_+·K` | `rank K > rank E_+` |\n| 4 `K·E_- → q⁻²·E_-·K` | `rank K > rank E_-` |\n| 5 `E_+·E_- → E_-·E_+ + …` | `rank E_+ > rank E_-` |\n| 6 `K⁻¹·E_+ → q⁻²·E_+·K⁻¹` | `rank K_inv > rank E_+` |\n| 7 `K⁻¹·E_- → q²·E_-·K⁻¹` | `rank K_inv > rank E_-` |\n\nRules 1 and 2 constrain nothing: their leading monomials beat `[]` on\nlength. This ranking satisfies all five, and `qSerre_lm_1 … qSerre_lm_7`\nprove every leading monomial outright, so the orientation is checked rather\nthan asserted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.instReprSU2Gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.instReprSU2Gen","kind":"instance","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.instReprSU2Gen.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.instReprSU2Gen.repr","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.instDecidableEqSU2Gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.instDecidableEqSU2Gen","kind":"instance","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SU2Gen.K_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SU2Gen.K_inv","kind":"ctor","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L50-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SU2Gen.K","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SU2Gen.K","kind":"ctor","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SU2Gen.E_minus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SU2Gen.E_minus","kind":"ctor","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L48-L48","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SU2Gen.E_plus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SU2Gen.E_plus","kind":"ctor","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SU2Gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SU2Gen","kind":"inductive","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/NormalForms.lean#L45-L51","doc":"The four generators of the quantum group `U_q(su(2))`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}